      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "2c7e99cc302f549ae2aa5789d253842900b939720acdd195c1de6e32868c7af2",
      "text": "Day 2 · City tour of Buenos Aires, often called the “Paris of South America”. Drive along Avenida 9 de Julio, one of the widest avenues in the world, with the Obelisk, symbol of the city, and stop at Plaza de Mayo to visit the Casa Rosada, the presidential palace, and the Metropolitan Cathedral, with its neoclassical façade and the mausoleum of the national hero General San Martín. The tour continues past Plaza San Martín, the Alvear area and Plaza del Congreso, along Avenida Corrientes and Avenida de Mayo, and through La Boca, San Telmo, Palermo, Recoleta and modern Puerto Madero.\n\nEvening · Dinner and tango show at Tango Porteño, a luxurious old theatre. Enjoy a three-course dinner of Argentine cuisine paired with traditional Argentine wines, soft drinks and water, then a live performance by professional dancers, singers and musicians recreating the golden age of tango in the 1940s, with meticulous scenery and costumes. Round-trip transfers in regular service included.",
